      <body>
         <entry xml:id="astrologia-dlgenr"
                xml:lang="en"
                type="mainEntry"
                prev="#astrologos-dlgenr"
                next="#istrateg-dlgenr"
                source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">אסטרולוגיא</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾsṭrwlwgyʾ</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">asṭrologiaʾ</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen" opt="false">f.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
               <form type="variant" opt="false">
                  <orth type="variant" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false">איסטרולוגיא</orth>
                  <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾsṭrwlwgyʾ</orth>
                  <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">isṭrologiaʾ</pron>
               </form>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="astrologia-dlgenr-1" opt="false">
               <usg type="domain" opt="false">sciences</usg>
               <usg type="socioCultural" norm="borrowing" opt="false">cultural borrowing</usg>
               <usg type="normativity" opt="false">standard</usg>
               <usg type="meaningType" opt="false">lit.</usg>
               <usg type="geographic" opt="false">Syriac Aramaic</usg>
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>astrology</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <usg opt="false">
                     <lang opt="false">Classical Greek</lang>
                  </usg>
                  <quote>ἀστρολογία</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>משל לאחד שהיה לו דין לפני שלטון ויצא דינו מלפני השלטון לישרף וצפה אותו השילטון 
                     <app>
                        <lem>באיסטרולוגיאה</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1">באצטרוגלייא</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox2">באסטרוגיליא</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#V">באסטרולוגיאה</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#K">באסטרוגוליא</rdg>
                     </app> שלו שהוא עתיד להוליד בת והיא נישאת למלך</quote>
                  <bibl default="false" status="draft">
                     <ref type="witness">63,2</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">II 679: 3</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>
                        This may be compared to a man who was on trial before the governor, and was sentenced by him to be burnt. But the governor foresaw by means of astrology that he was destined to beget a daughter who would  marry the king… (Cf. Freedman / Simon II 557)
            </quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note anchored="true">= <bibl type="ancient">Yаlq 110 [II 511: 85]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אסטרולוגוס</term>); 
            <bibl type="ancient" default="false" status="draft">LevR 36,4</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אצטרוגליס</term>);
                     <bibl type="ancient" default="false" status="draft">Yalq Jes 436 [XI 145: 54]</bibl>
                  </note>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>דאמר ר' יהושע בן לוי רואה היית 
                     <app>
                        <lem>באיסטרולוגיאה</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1">באסתרגלין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#K">באסטרוגילין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox2">באיצטרוגילין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat1">באסטרולוגין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat2">באיסטרולוגין</rdg>
                     </app> שלה שעתידה להעמיד ממנו בן</quote>
                  <bibl default="false" status="draft">
                     <ref type="witness">85,2</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">II 1031: 4</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>
                        For R. Yehoshuaʿ b. Lewi said: She [Potiphar’s wife] saw by her astrological arts that she was to produce a child by him  [Joseph]... (Freedman / Simon II 788)
            </quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note anchored="true">=
                     <bibl type="ancient" default="false" status="draft">Yalq 144 [II 732: 44]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">איסטרולוגין</term>);
            <bibl type="ancient" default="false" status="draft">YalqM Jes 47,13 [165: 29]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">איצטרוגלין</term>)
         </note>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>ר' מנחמה בש' ר' ביבי כך ווסתן של אומות העולם, כיון שהיה אחד מהן לוקח לו עבד, היה הולך אצל {אסטרולוגוס} ואמ' ליה חנא טבא נחשא טבא, אין לשון הזה ותשא אלא לשון 
                     <app>
                     <lem>אסטרולוגיאה</lem>
                     <rdg wit="#Vat1">אסטרולגייה</rdg>
                     <rdg wit="#Ox1">איסטרגליא</rdg>
                     <rdg wit="#Ox2">אסטרוגליא</rdg>
                     <rdg wit="#K V">איסטרוגילין</rdg>
                     <rdg wit="#Vat2">איסטרולוגיה</rdg>
                  </app> , כמה דאת אמ' ופן תשא עיניך השמימה וגו'</quote>
                  <bibl default="false" status="draft">
                     <ref type="witness">87,4</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">III 1065: 1</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa" target="astrologos.html">אסטרולוגוס</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>
                        R. Menaḥema said in R. Bibi’s name: This was the practice of the heathens. When one bought a man slave, he would go to an astrologer, who would tell him, ‘If you acquire a good bondmaid, it is an auspicious augury.’ Thus wa-tiśśaʾ (cast her eyes) [Gen 39,7] is a term used of astrology, as in the verse, And lest thou lift up (tiśśaʾ) thine eyes unto heaven etc. (Dtn 4,19) (Freedman / Simon II 808)
            </quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note anchored="true">=
            <bibl type="ancient" default="false" status="draft">Yalq 145 [46b: 59]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אסטרולוגיא</term>)
         </note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <etym type="borrowing" opt="false">
               <lbl opt="false">source language</lbl>
               <lang opt="false">Classical Greek+</lang>
               <cit type="etymon" xml:lang="grc">
                  <xr type="related" opt="false">
                     <lbl opt="false">Cf. LSJ</lbl>
                     <ref target="https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/morph?l=a)stro-logi/a"
                          type="entry">ἀστρολογία</ref>
                  </xr>
               </cit>
            </etym>
            <note anchored="true">Cf.
      <bibl type="modern" default="false" status="draft">AC I 176ab</bibl>;
      <bibl type="modern" default="false" status="draft">Levy I 123ab</bibl>;
      <bibl type="modern" default="false" status="draft">Krauss, LW II 122ab</bibl>;
      <bibl type="modern" default="false" status="draft">Jastrow I 91b</bibl>. Frequently corr. <term xml:lang="jpa">אסטרוגוליא</term>
               <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾsṭrwgwlyʾ</term>
               <term xml:lang="rabbinic">a(i)sṭrogoliaʾ</term>. Levy and Jastrow consider the reading <term xml:lang="jpa">אסטרולוגין</term>
               <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾsṭrwlwgyn</term>
               <term xml:lang="rabbinic">a(i)sṭrologin</term> in Vat 1 (and other) for GenR 85,2 as pl., but cf. Krauss. For Syr. <term xml:lang="syc">ܐܣܛܪܘܠܘܓܝܐ</term>
               <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾsṭrwlwgyʾ</term> cf.
      <bibl type="modern" default="false" status="draft">Sokoloff, SL 70b</bibl>. Cf.
      <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">אסטרולוג</ref>
            </note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl default="false" status="draft">
                  <title>Sokoloff, DJPA</title>
                  <citedRange>25b</citedRange>
               </bibl>
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>122ab</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
